{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm settling on a design where `double_underline` is a new name mapped to the same bit as `underline2`, so the existing behavior stays intact. The open question is what `str(style)` should return: keeping \"underline2\" is the safer choice for regression tests, but the spec seems to want \"double_underline\" to take precedence.\n\nI'm weighing whether to keep \"underline2\" as the str output for regression safety, and I still need to check the spec's stance on \"double_underline\". Next I want to see how `get_html_style` handles bit 9, so I'll look at the end of style.py and the export_svg section.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"Existing `underline2` is SGR 21, which is double underline, so I'll add `double_underline` as a first-class name mapped to the same bit rather than a second bit. Next I need the HTML and SVG CSS paths and the parser."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KR5m1hGm4q41aPhye9XYBc","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && grep -n \"def get_html_style\\|def parse\\|def combine\\|def __add__\\|def _add\\|_Bit\\|class _Bit\" rich/style.py; sed -n 500,540p rich/style.py; echo ----; grep -n \"def get_html_style\" -A40 rich/style.py | head -60; echo ----; sed -n 2370,2410p rich/console.py; echo ----; grep -n \"underline\\|text-decoration\" rich/_export_format.py rich/*.py | grep -v emoji | head"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":570,"cacheRead":6200,"cacheWrite":5984,"totalTokens":12756,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.000285,"cacheRead":0.000062,"cacheWrite":0.000748,"total":0.0010952,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":274},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794167146146,"providerThinkingLevel":"medium","responseId":"msg_011