{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The HTML/SVG export doesn't handle double underline yet, so I need to add it. Emitting both \"underline\" and \"underline double\" would let the latter win in CSS, so I'll pick one: \"underline double\" when double is set, otherwise plain \"underline\". Strikethrough and overline also write to text-decoration, so I have to check how they combine with that.\n\nI'm weighing whether to keep the double-underline check ahead of the plain underline branch so the two don't collide in the CSS. I'll also look at how strikethrough and overline combine with the same text-decoration property, then check the parse and combine logic and the existing test expectations.\n\nI'm settling how to handle the double-underline attribute, since the Style constructor and the existing `underline2` alias both need to work with the new name. I'll compute a single value from either parameter, so whichever one is passed gets used in both places. I'm also leaving the `str` output and repr as they are so the existing tests keep passing.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"The HTML and SVG exporters ignore bit 9 entirely, so both need a new rule. Before editing I'll check the parser tail, `combine`/`_add`, and the existing test expectations so I don't break `str()` output."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01PakjuAUDp4UYuT4VCz9Bmk","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && sed -n 540,562p rich/style.py; echo ----; sed -n 600,625p rich/style.py; sed -n 733,760p rich/style.py; echo ----; sed -n 20,60p tests/test_style.py; grep -n \"_hash_getter\" -A8 rich/style.py | head -12"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1032,"cacheRead":12184,"cacheWrite":2789,"totalTokens":16007,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"outp